{"chapter": "formal-defos", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "06SX", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{F}$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:5407f3381e3c59fb1dafb63aa5ce9f34521fbfecefbfaecbd978d086d68efb5c", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:aefc2fe6d8968ab1c90a393930ed1cc1fec0f78e30bb8ed78f4dd15ecb553b19", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nThe existence of a versal formal object forces <MATH_0001> to have\nproperty (S1).\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:bfe04bf53460b912b55be231bb82a16fd4085bb0aaac6e2f61a85bf3952188fb", "unit_id": "tag:06SX:prose-0001"}
{"chapter": "formal-defos", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "06SX", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{F}$", "MATH_0002": "$\\mathcal{F}$", "MATH_0003": "$\\mathcal{F}$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-versal-object-S1}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:09cb624634d57f425d2526f59926e98beac689424e0a4e57b1dc4d394e6c680a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:707799bfb0e46dd39f9b19705d1ffb4a4b05c388b128307b5e59d452b44ec55f", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a predeformation category.\nAssume <MATH_0002> has a versal formal object.\nThen <MATH_0003> satisfies (S1).\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:54465abc88e8ee3fe5eeb700d6210a659dbf42d275eb9522ba55eee5240cbdd0", "unit_id": "tag:06SY:statement"}
{"chapter": "formal-defos", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "06SX", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\xi$", "MATH_0002": "$\\mathcal{F}$", "MATH_0003": "$$\n\\xymatrix{\n           & x_2 \\ar[d] \\\\\nx_1 \\ar[r] & x\n}\n$$", "MATH_0004": "$\\mathcal{F}$", "MATH_0005": "$x_2 \\to x$", "MATH_0006": "$\\widehat{\\mathcal{F}}|_{\\mathcal{C}_\\Lambda} \\xrightarrow{\\sim} \\mathcal{F}$", "MATH_0007": "$\\widehat{\\mathcal{F}}$", "MATH_0008": "$\\xi \\to x_1$", "MATH_0009": "$\\xi \\to x_2$", "MATH_0010": "$$\n\\xymatrix{\n\\xi \\ar[r] \\ar[d]          & x_2 \\ar[d] \\\\\nx_1 \\ar[r] & x\n}\n$$", "MATH_0011": "$x_1 \\to x$", "MATH_0012": "$x_2 \\to x$", "MATH_0013": "$A_1 \\to A$", "MATH_0014": "$A_2 \\to A$", "MATH_0015": "$\\xi$", "MATH_0016": "$A_1 \\times_A A_2$", "MATH_0017": "$y$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{remark-restrict-completion}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{lemma-versal-object-quasi-initial}", "REF_0003": "\\ref{remark-versal-object}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:5bee12fd1c6f86550fe3d6e02e632aa58901684f09f8ed098e0b31ec87f4455f", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:32e5af262800af6d92af385a871fef6a90600e08f9704f925f6c800ac1e70d74", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a versal formal object of <MATH_0002>. Let\n<MATH_0003>\nbe a diagram in <MATH_0004> such that <MATH_0005> lies over a\nsurjective ring map. Since the natural morphism\n<MATH_0006>\nis an equivalence (see\nRemark <REF_0001>), we can consider this\ndiagram also as a diagram in <MATH_0007>. By\nLemma <REF_0002> there exists a morphism\n<MATH_0008>, so by\nRemark <REF_0003> we also get a\nmorphism <MATH_0009> making the diagram\n<MATH_0010>\ncommute. If <MATH_0011> and <MATH_0012> lie above ring maps\n<MATH_0013> and <MATH_0014> then taking the pushforward of\n<MATH_0015> to <MATH_0016> gives an object <MATH_0017> as required by (S1).\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:8857359b1f5110ae9a52f86d514c5de278859517f206ed2fb9da1374c6d823c5", "unit_id": "tag:06SY:proof"}
{"chapter": "formal-defos", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "06SX", "placeholders": {"STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:dedd8e6f0ec7d6f5ace0e02ece4f7a390ed65247ea32f2479cfcd4564817a41c", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nIn the case that our cofibred category satisfies (S1) and (S2)\nwe can characterize the versal formal objects as follows.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:5cfcfaf1b2bb1f80eefb4c6509e9026226a3e4eaba4f28bb0eb98eb2ed3cfcb4", "unit_id": "tag:06SX:prose-0002"}
